.SH NAME
CWE\-345 \- Insufficient Verification of Data Authenticity
.SH RANK
KEV\-referenced weakness. Not part of the 2025 CWE Top 25; documented here because it appears in the CISA KEV catalog.
.SH CLASSIFICATION
Class: KEV\-referenced weakness.
.SH DESCRIPTION
The product does not sufficiently verify the origin or authenticity of data, in a way that causes it to accept invalid data.
.SH KNOWN EXPLOITED VULNERABILITIES
CISA KEV catalog (as of 2026-11-15): \fB1\fR exploited CVE mapped to this weakness. Each entry has the catalog write\-up of how it was used in the wild (not a runnable exploit) and the required remediation. Code\-level vulnerable\->fixed pairs, when curated, are under \fBEXAMPLES\fR.
.SS CVE\-2026\-111357
Ivanti Connect Secure, added 2026\-10\-30.
.PP
Ivanti Connect Secure Missing Authentication for Critical Function Vulnerability.
.PP
\fIHow it is exploited (CISA):\fR
Ivanti Connect Secure contains a missing authentication for critical function vulnerability that could allow a local authenticated attacker to escalate their privileges. This vulnerability can be chained with CVE\-2026\-104935 and CVE\-2026\-118527.
.PP
\fIRemediation:\fR
Apply vendor mitigations; follow CISA BOD 26\-04 (risk\-based patching) and forensics triage. Discontinue use if no mitigation exists.
 Due 2026\-11\-02.
.PP
